              "section": "1.1",
              "subsection": "1.1.2",
              "rawText": "Deﬁnition 4 Let p and q be propositions. The exclusive or of p and q, denoted by p⊕q (or p XOR q), is\nthe proposition that is true when exactly one of p and q is true and is false otherwise.",
              "text": "Definition 4 Let p and q be propositions. The exclusive or of p and q, denoted by p⊕q (or p XOR q), is the proposition that is true when exactly one of p and q is true and is false otherwise.",
