              "kind": "text",
              "section": "1.2",
              "subsection": "1.2.3",
              "rawText": "Translating sentences in natural language (such as English) into logical expressions is an essen-\ntial part of specifying both hardware and software systems. System and software engineers take\nrequirements in natural language and produce precise and unambiguous speciﬁcations that can\nbe used as the basis for system development. Example 3 shows how compound propositions can\nbe used in this process.",
              "text": "Translating sentences in natural language (such as English) into logical expressions is an essential part of specifying both hardware and software systems. System and software engineers take requirements in natural language and produce precise and unambiguous specifications that can be used as the basis for system development. Example 3 shows how compound propositions can be used in this process.",
