              "kind": "example",
              "section": "1.2",
              "subsection": "1.2.3",
              "rawText": "EXAMPLE 3 Express the speciﬁcation “The automated reply cannot be sent when the ﬁle system is full”\nusing logical connectives.\nSolution: One way to translate this is to letp denote “The automated reply can be sent” andq de-\nnote “The ﬁle system is full.” Then ¬p represents “It is not the case that the automated reply can\nExtra \nExamples\nbe sent,” which can also be expressed as “The automated reply cannot be sent.” Consequently,\nour speciﬁcation can be represented by the conditional statement q → ¬p. ◂",
