              "section": "1.4",
              "subsection": "1.4.4",
              "rawText": "Similarly, when the elements of the domain are x1,x 2,… ,x n, where n is a positive integer,\nthe existential quantiﬁcation ∃xP(x) is the same as the disjunction\nP(x1)∨P(x2)∨⋯ ∨P(xn),\nbecause this disjunction is true if and only if at least one of P(x1),P (x2),… ,P (xn) is true.",
              "text": "Similarly, when the elements of the domain are x1,x 2,… ,x n, where n is a positive integer, the existential quantification ∃xP(x) is the same as the disjunction P(x1)∨P(x2)∨⋯ ∨P(xn), because this disjunction is true if and only if at least one of P(x1),P (x2),… ,P (xn) is true.",
