              "rawText": "The quantiﬁers ∀and ∃have higher precedence than all logical operators from propositional\ncalculus. For example, ∀xP(x)∨Q(x) is the disjunction of ∀xP(x) and Q(x). In other words, it\nmeans (∀xP(x))∨Q(x) rather than ∀x(P(x)∨Q(x)).",
