              "kind": "remark",
              "section": "1.6",
              "subsection": "1.6.2",
              "rawText": "Remark: From the deﬁnition of a valid argument form we see that the argument form with\npremises p\n1, p2,… ,p n and conclusion q is valid exactly when (p 1 ∧p2 ∧⋯ ∧pn) → q is a\ntautology.",
              "text": "Remark: From the definition of a valid argument form we see that the argument form with premises p 1, p2,… ,p n and conclusion q is valid exactly when (p 1 ∧p2 ∧⋯ ∧pn) → q is a tautology.",
