              "rawText": "Deﬁnition 2 The real number r is rational if there exist integers p and q with q ≠ 0 such that r = p∕q.A\nreal number that is not rational is called irrational.",
              "text": "Definition 2 The real number r is rational if there exist integers p and q with q ≠ 0 such that r = p∕q.A real number that is not rational is called irrational.",
