              "kind": "text",
              "section": "1.7",
              "subsection": "1.7.8",
              "rawText": "Making mistakes in proofs is part of the learning process. When you make a mistake that\nsomeone else ﬁnds, you should carefully analyze where you went wrong and make sure that\nyou do not make the same mistake again. Even professional mathematicians make mistakes in\nproofs. More than a few incorrect proofs of important results have fooled people for many years\nbefore subtle errors in them were found.",
