              "subsection": "1.8.5",
              "rawText": "ADAPTING EXISTING PROOFS An excellent way to look for possible approaches that can\nbe used to prove a statement is to take advantage of existing proofs of similar results. Often\nan existing proof can be adapted to prove other facts. Even when this is not the case, some of\nthe ideas used in existing proofs may be helpful. Because existing proofs provide clues for new\nproofs, you should read and understand the proofs you encounter in your studies. This process\nis illustrated in Example 16.",
              "text": "ADAPTING EXISTING PROOFS An excellent way to look for possible approaches that can be used to prove a statement is to take advantage of existing proofs of similar results. Often an existing proof can be adapted to prove other facts. Even when this is not the case, some of the ideas used in existing proofs may be helpful. Because existing proofs provide clues for new proofs, you should read and understand the proofs you encounter in your studies. This process is illustrated in Example 16.",
