              "rawText": "Remark: The equation x2 + y2 = z2 has inﬁnitely many solutions in integers x, y, and z; theseLinks solutions are called Pythagorean triples and correspond to the lengths of the sides of right tri-\nangles with integer lengths. See Exercise 34.",
