        "rawText": "Deﬁnition 1 An argument in propositional logic is a sequence of propositions. All but the ﬁnal proposition\nin the argument are called premises and the ﬁnal proposition is called the conclusion.A n\nargument is valid if the truth of all its premises implies that the conclusion is true.",
