        "rawText": "Deﬁnition 1 The integern is even if there exists an integerk such that n = 2k, and n is odd if there exists an\ninteger k such that n = 2k+ 1. (Note that every integer is either even or odd, and no integer\nis both even and odd.) Two integers have thesame parity when both are even or both are odd;\nthey have opposite parity when one is even and the other is odd.",
        "text": "Definition 1 The integern is even if there exists an integerk such that n = 2k, and n is odd if there exists an integer k such that n = 2k+ 1. (Note that every integer is either even or odd, and no integer is both even and odd.) Two integers have thesame parity when both are even or both are odd; they have opposite parity when one is even and the other is odd.",
